$ todoer add fix-login -l auth
.todoer/todos/fix-login.md

$ todoer labels rule auth 'Add this label to a todo that changes the login.'
.todoer/labels/auth.md

$ printf 'Add it to a todo that changes the docs.\nNot to a typo fix.\n' | todoer labels rule docs
.todoer/labels/docs.md

--- .todoer/labels/docs.md
Add it to a todo that changes the docs.
Not to a typo fix.

$ todoer labels rule auth --rm extra
exit code: 1
--- stderr
error: use: todoer labels rule <label> [text] | todoer labels rule <label> --rm

$ todoer labels rule Auth 'A rule.'
exit code: 1
--- stderr
error: "Auth" is not a label - use lowercase letters, digits and hyphens

$ todoer labels rule ui < /dev/null
exit code: 1
--- stderr
error: the rule of ui has no text - give the text, or pipe it on stdin

$ todoer labels rule ui --rm
exit code: 1
--- stderr
error: the label ui has no rule - run todoer labels

$ todoer labels --rm
exit code: 1
--- stderr
error: use: todoer labels [--json]

$ todoer add login-page
.todoer/todos/login-page.md
check the label rules: todoer labels

$ todoer labels
auth  1 todo
  Add this label to a todo that changes the login.
docs  0 todos
  Add it to a todo that changes the docs.
  Not to a typo fix.

$ todoer labels --json
[
  {
    "label": "auth",
    "todos": 1,
    "rule": "Add this label to a todo that changes the login."
  },
  {
    "label": "docs",
    "todos": 0,
    "rule": "Add it to a todo that changes the docs.\nNot to a typo fix."
  }
]

$ todoer labels mv auth docs
exit code: 1
--- stderr
error: auth and docs both have a rule - remove one rule first: todoer labels rule <label> --rm

$ todoer labels mv auth security
fix-login: renamed the label auth -> security
renamed the rule auth -> security

$ todoer labels mv docs guides
renamed the rule docs -> guides

$ todoer labels mv missing other
exit code: 1
--- stderr
error: no todo and no rule has the label missing - run todoer labels

$ todoer labels
guides    0 todos
  Add it to a todo that changes the docs.
  Not to a typo fix.
security  1 todo
  Add this label to a todo that changes the login.

$ todoer labels rule security --rm
removed the rule of security

$ todoer labels rm guides
removed the rule of guides

$ todoer labels rm security
fix-login: removed the label security

$ todoer labels
no labels

$ todoer check
2 todos and 0 label rules, no problems

$ todoer check
exit code: 1
.todoer/labels/Bad.md: "Bad" is not a label - use lowercase letters, digits and hyphens
.todoer/labels/empty.md: the rule is empty - write the rule, or run todoer labels rule empty --rm
.todoer/labels/notes.txt: not a rule - name the file <label>.md
--- stderr
error: 3 problems in 2 todos and 1 label rule

$ todoer labels
empty  0 todos
--- stderr
warning: .todoer/labels/Bad.md: "Bad" is not a label - use lowercase letters, digits and hyphens
warning: .todoer/labels/empty.md: the rule is empty - write the rule, or run todoer labels rule empty --rm
warning: .todoer/labels/notes.txt: not a rule - name the file <label>.md

